{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01KSWZGHd8huVqFNezeUSAH2","toolName":"subagent","args":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nCLI file: src/cli.ts\nPassing tests: 38 (all)\nRecent changes: added runScenario() orchestration (processes quote/claim steps sequentially, tracks per-policy remainingCap, counts prior quotes for follow-up discount), validateDamages() (rejects negative amounts, unknown types, and more damages of a type than covered), and KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES set. cli.ts reads stdin JSON, calls runScenario, writes results, exits non-zero with stderr on errors.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Focus on runScenario/validateDamages readability. Do NOT change behavior.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 38 tests pass. Now let me analyze and refactor `runScenario`/`validateDamages`.\n\n## Naming Evaluation (First Priority)\n\n- `runScenario` — clearly describes orchestrating a scenario's steps. **Keep.**\n- `validateDamages` — accurately describes rejecting invalid damage entries. **Keep.**\n- Inside `runScenario`, the quote branch has an **inline unnamed loop** that validates item types — its intent is hidden. This mirrors what `validateDamages` does for claims but is not named symmetrically.\n\n## APP Mass — `validateDamages` (before)\n\nCounting-by-type map is built inline, duplicating the \"count items by type\" concept also seen in `basePremium`.\n\n- Bindings: `covered`, `item`, `items`, `claimed`, `damage`, `damages` ≈ 6\n- Constants: `{}`×2, `0`×2, `1`×2, messages×3 ≈ 9\n- Invocations: `.has`×2, `??`×3, template strings ≈ ~7 → 14\n- Conditionals: 3 `if` + 3 `??` used as guards ≈ 4×3 = 12 (counting the 3 `if`s)\n- Loops: 2 → 10\n- Assignments: 2 → 12\n\nRough total ≈ **60+**. The two count-map constructions are conceptual duplication (Rule 3).\n\n## Refactorings\n\n**1. (Rule 2/3)** Extract a named `validateItemTypes` helper and reuse it in the quote branch — reveals intent and removes the hidden inline loop.\n**2. (Rule 3)** Extract `countByType` to remove the duplicated \"count-by-type\" logic."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nCLI file: src/cli.ts\nPassing tests: 38 (all)\nRecent changes: added runScenario() orchestration (processes quote/claim steps sequentially, tracks per-policy remainingCap, counts prior quotes for follow-up discount), validateDamages() (rejects negative amounts, unknown types, and more damages of a type than covered), and KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES set. cli.ts reads stdin JSON, calls runScenario, writes results, exits non-zero with stderr on errors.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Focus on runScenario/validateDamages readability. Do NOT change behavior.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nCLI file: src/cli.ts\nPassing tests: 38 (all)\nRecent changes: added runScenario() orchestration (processes quote/claim steps sequentially, tracks per-policy remainingCap, counts prior quotes for follow-up discount), validateDamages() (rejects negative amounts, unknown types, and more damages of a type than covered), and KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES set. cli.ts reads stdin JSON, calls runScenario, writes results, exits non-zero with stderr on errors.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Focus on runScenario/validateDamages readability. Do NOT change behavior.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784909796907},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the implementation and test files to understand how everything works together.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_011kA5MJEpea8r5WMZD6Ta3J","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Gb3wTHQHRnVHQrwj7YDMtE","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/cli.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":341,"output":254,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10299,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909796927,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8a89946a-4058-42eb-a16d-e827640db26b","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_011kA5MJEpea8r5WMZD6Ta3J","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst FOLLOWUP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst itemBasePremium = (item: Item): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) return COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  return BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n};\n\nconst itemSurcharges = (item: Item): number => {\n  let surcharge = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) surcharge += itemBasePremium(item) * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    surcharge += itemBasePremium(item) * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  }\n  return surcharge;\n};\n\nconst componentBasePremium = (count: number): number => {\n  if (count === BLOCK_SIZE) return BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  return count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n};\n\nconst itemSurchargeTotal = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + itemSurcharges(item), 0);\n\nconst basePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      total += BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    }\n  }\n  for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n    total += componentBasePremium(count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: Item[],\n  priorContracts: number\n): number => {\n  const base = basePremium(items);\n  const modifier = (rate: number, applies: boolean): number =>\n    applies ? base * rate : 0;\n\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = modifier(FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE, true);\n  const loyaltyDiscount = modifier(\n    LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE,\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD\n  );\n  const followupDiscount = modifier(FOLLOWUP_DISCOUNT_RATE, priorContracts > 0);\n\n  const premium =\n    base +\n    itemSurchargeTotal(items) +\n    firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n    loyaltyDiscount -\n    followupDiscount +\n    PROCESSING_FEE;\n\n  return Math.ceil(premium);\n};\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\n\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\nconst INSURANCE_VALUE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n};\nconst COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE = 250;\n\nconst itemInsuranceValue = (item: Item): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) return COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE;\n  return INSURANCE_VALUE[item.type] ?? 0;\n};\n\nexport const insuranceSum = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + itemInsuranceValue(item), 0);\n};\n\nexport const cap = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  return insuranceSum(items) * CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n};\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst damageReimbursement = (items: Item[], damage: Damage): number => {\n  const item = items.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n  const isHighEnchantment =\n    (item?.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD;\n  const covered = isHighEnchantment\n    ? damage.amount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE\n    : damage.amount;\n  return Math.max(0, covered - DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nexport const claim = (\n  items: Item[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  remainingCap: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const reimbursableTotal = damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + damageReimbursement(items, damage),\n    0\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(Math.floor(reimbursableTotal), remainingCap);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n};\n\nconst KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\n  \"sword\",\n  \"amulet\",\n  \"staff\",\n  \"potion\",\n  \"rune\",\n  \"moonstone\",\n]);\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: Damage[] };\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport type StepResult =\n  | { premium: number }\n  | { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\n\ninterface Policy {\n  items: Item[];\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): StepResult[] => {\n  const { customer, steps } = scenario;\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  const policies: Record<number, Policy> = {};\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n\n  steps.forEach((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      for (const item of step.items) {\n        if (!KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n        }\n      }\n      const premium = quote(customer, step.items, quoteCount);\n      quoteCount += 1;\n      policies[index] = { items: step.items, remainingCap: cap(step.items) };\n      results.push({ premium });\n    } else {\n      const policy = policies[step.policy];\n      if (!policy) {\n        throw new Error(`No policy at step ${step.policy}`);\n      }\n      const { damages } = step.incident;\n      validateDamages(policy.items, damages);\n      const result = claim(policy.items, damages, policy.remainingCap);\n      policy.remainingCap = result.remainingCap;\n      results.push(result);\n    }\n  });\n\n  return results;\n};\n\nconst validateDamages = (items: Item[], damages: Damage[]): void => {\n  const covered: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    covered[item.type] = (covered[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n  }\n  const claimed: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const damage of damages) {\n    if (damage.amount < 0) {\n      throw new Error(`Negative damage amount: ${damage.amount}`);\n    }\n    if (!KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES.has(damage.itemType)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${damage.itemType}`);\n    }\n    claimed[damage.itemType] = (claimed[damage.itemType] ?? 0) + 1;\n    if ((claimed[damage.itemType] ?? 0) > (covered[damage.itemType] ?? 0)) {\n      throw new Error(`Damage to uninsured item: ${damage.itemType}`);\n    }\n  }\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909799910},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Gb3wTHQHRnVHQrwj7YDMtE","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env node\nimport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { runScenario, Scenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\nconst main = (): void => {\n  const raw = readFileSync(0, \"utf8\");\n  const scenario = JSON.parse(raw) as Scenario;\n  const results = runScenario(scenario);\n  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ results }) + \"\\n\");\n};\n\ntry {\n  main();\n} catch (error) {\n  const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n  process.stderr.write(`Error: ${message}\\n`);\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909799910},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me run the tests to make sure everything's passing.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_016gLNyZer5tjwdFX1pQBxzh","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -15"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":3978,"output":149,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13831,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909799910,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-eed6644d-ef62-4d6f-834b-f420381d95dd","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_016gLNyZer5tjwdFX1pQBxzh","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking\n\nError: Unknown item type: broomstick\nError: Damage to unin