`×2, `0`×2, `1`×2, messages×3 ≈ 9\n- Invocations: `.has`×2, `??`×3, template strings ≈ ~7 → 14\n- Conditionals: 3 `if` + 3 `??` used as guards ≈ 4×3 = 12 (counting the 3 `if`s)\n- Loops: 2 → 10\n- Assignments: 2 → 12\n\nRough total ≈ **60+**. The two count-map constructions are conceptual duplication (Rule 3).\n\n## Refactorings\n\n**1. (Rule 2/3)** Extract a named `validateItemTypes` helper and reuse it in the quote branch — reveals intent and removes the hidden inline loop.\n**2. (Rule 3)** Extract `countByType` to remove the duplicated \"count-by-type\" logic."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01QB6zWgFTdgiYY3yd5amR38","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\n  \"sword\",\n  \"amulet\",\n  \"staff\",\n  \"potion\",\n  \"rune\",\n  \"moonstone\",\n]);","newText":"const KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\n  \"sword\",\n  \"amulet\",\n  \"staff\",\n  \"potion\",\n  \"rune\",\n  \"moonstone\",\n]);\n\nconst countByType = (items: Item[]): Record<string, number> => {\n  const counts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts[item.type] = (counts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst validateItemTypes = (items: Item[]): void => {\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (!KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n    }\n  }\n};"},{"oldText":"    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      for (const item of step.items) {\n        if (!KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n        }\n      }\n      const premium = quote(customer, step.items, quoteCount);","newText":"    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      validateItemTypes(step.items);\n      const premium = quote(customer, step.items, quoteCount);"},{"oldText":"const validateDamages = (items: Item[], damages: Damage[]): void => {\n  const covered: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    covered[item.type] = (covered[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n  }\n  const claimed: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const damage of damages) {\n    if (damage.amount < 0) {\n      throw new Error(`Negative damage amount: ${damage.amount}`);\n    }\n    if (!KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES.has(damage.itemType)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${damage.itemType}`);\n    }\n    claimed[damage.itemType] = (claimed[damage.itemType] ?? 0) + 1;\n    if ((claimed[damage.itemType] ?? 0) > (covered[damage.itemType] ?? 0)) {\n      throw new Error(`Damage to uninsured item: ${damage.itemType}`);\n    }\n  }\n};","newText":"const validateDamages = (items: Item[], damages: Damage[]): void => {\n  const coveredCounts = countByType(items);\n  const claimedCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const damage of damages) {\n    if (damage.amount < 0) {\n      throw new Error(`Negative damage amount: ${damage.amount}`);\n    }\n    if (!KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES.has(damage.itemType)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${damage.itemType}`);\n    }\n    claimedCounts[damage.itemType] =\n      (claimedCounts[damage.itemType] ?? 0) + 1;\n    if (claimedCounts[damage.itemType] > (coveredCounts[damage.itemType] ?? 0)) {\n      throw new Error(`Damage to uninsured item: ${damage.itemType}`);\n    }\n  }\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":4382,"output":2795,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":16881,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909805496,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-e922c8e0-60b5-43ec-b746-913b3b39ab9e","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01QB6zWgFTdgiYY3yd5amR38","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replac