Rule 3 (No Duplication): no duplication present.\n- Rule 4 (Fewest Elements): `quote` reduced to its essential elements.\n\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `basePremium(items)` helper; `quote` simplified to a linear pipeline.\n**Mass Change**: `quote` body ~96 → ~13 (logic relocated, not duplicated).\n**Tests**: All 11 passing."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 11\nRecent changes: quote() now counts components per type (rune/moonstone) via COMPONENT_TYPES set, applies block pricing (exactly 3 -> 60) per type, main items summed from BASE_PREMIUM.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 11\nRecent changes: quote() now counts components per type (rune/moonstone) via COMPONENT_TYPES set, applies block pricing (exactly 3 -> 60) per type, main items summed from BASE_PREMIUM.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784909174016},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll refactor the implementation. Let me first read the current state of both files."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01NiqLyuG2Euw4nfFNxSXK45","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_019QKfj6q2scBjbFEhwrFdwr","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":224,"output":130,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10058,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909174035,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-40018811-521b-4a35-a7de-9db9e6daaa7f","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01NiqLyuG2Euw4nfFNxSXK45","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst componentBasePremium = (count: number): number => {\n  if (count === BLOCK_SIZE) return BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  return count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n};\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: Item[],\n  priorContracts: number\n): number => {\n  let basePremiumTotal = 0;\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      basePremiumTotal += BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    }\n  }\n  for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n    basePremiumTotal += componentBasePremium(count);\n  }\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge =\n    basePremiumTotal * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  return Math.ceil(basePremiumTotal + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nexport const claim = (): number => {\n  return undefined as unknown as number;\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909175814},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_019QKfj6q2scBjbFEhwrFdwr","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote, claim } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office - quote\", () => {\n  // Empty / processing fee\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [], 0)).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  // Base premiums for main items (newcomer 0 years: base + first insurance 10% + fee)\n  it(\"single sword (newcomer) -> base 100 + 10 first-insurance + 5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"sword\" }], 0)).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet (newcomer) -> base 60 + 6 + 5 = 71 G\", () => {\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"amulet\" }], 0)).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"single staff (newcomer) -> base 80 + 8 + 5 = 93 G\", () => {\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"staff\" }], 0)).toBe(93);\n  });\n  it(\"single potion (newcomer) -> base 40 + 4 + 5 = 49 G\", () => {\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"potion\" }], 0)).toBe(49);\n  });\n\n  // Component base premiums / building block of 3 alike components\n  it(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium\", () => {\n    // newcomer: base 50 + 5 first-insurance + 5 fee = 60\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }], 0)).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies)\", () => {\n    // block base 60 + 6 first-insurance + 5 fee = 71\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }], 0)).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block - block requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    // 4*25=100 + 10 first-insurance + 5 fee = 115\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }], 0)).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium\", () => {\n    // 7*25=175 + 17.5 first-insurance + 5 fee = 197.5 -> ceil 198\n    const items = Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" }));\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, items, 0)).toBe(198);\n  });\n\n  // \"Alike\" components\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G base premium (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    // 3*25=75 + 7.5 first-insurance + 5 fee = 87.5 -> ceil 88\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }], 0)).toBe(88);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G base premium (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    // 60 + 60 = 120 + 12 first-insurance + 5 fee = 137\n    const items = [\n      { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ];\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, items, 0)).toBe(137);\n  });\n\n  // Cursed / high enchantment surcharges in isolation (newcomer)\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (steel, ench 3), newcomer -> 165 G (integration example)\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment 5 -> both surcharges apply\");\n\n  // Modifier scope on multi-item policies\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword + plain amulet -> curse surcharge = 50% of cursed item base only, 210 G before modifiers/fee\");\n\n  // Loyalty discount threshold\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years -> loyalty discount applies\");\n\n  // Follow-up contract discount + integration example\n  it.todo(\"long-standing customer's second contract (cursed sword ench 7, 3 years) -> 160 G\");\n\n  // Rounding in favor\n  it.todo(\"premium calculation yielding 197.5 -> final premium 198 (rounded up)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office - claim\", () => {\n  // Standard reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"regular sword (steel, ench 3), damage 500 -> payout 400 (full - 100 deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"rune (value 250), damage 200 -> payout 100 (full - 100 deductible)\");\n\n  // High enchantment reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"steel sword, ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% then deductible)\");\n\n  // Dragon material reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword, ench 5, damage 800 -> payout 700 (full then deductible)\");\n\n  // Both clauses -> 50% wins\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword, ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% wins, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword, exactly ench 8, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (high-ench then deductible)\");\n\n  // Deductible per damage event\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages sword (500) and amulet (300) -> payout 600 (deductible per item)\");\n\n  // Insurance sum and cap\n  it.todo(\"policy covers two swords -> insurance sum 2000, cap 4000\");\n  it.todo(\"policy covers sword + amulet -> insurance sum 1600, cap 3200\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (premium 165) -> cap 2000 (based on unmodified insurance value)\");\n  it.todo(\"policy covers sword + 3 runes block -> insurance sum 1750 (block only affects premium)\");\n\n  // Multiple items of same type\n  it.todo(\"two swords, dragon attack damages both -> each damage own deductible\");\n\n  // Cap exhaustion across successive claims\n  it.todo(\"sword (cap 2000), two claims of 1500 each -> first payout 1400 (cap rem 600), second payout 600 (cap rem 0)\");\n\n  // Payout rounding\n  it.todo(\"payout calculation yielding 350.5 -> final payout 350 (rounded down)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office - CLI / errors\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"quote with unknown item type -> non-zero exit, error to stderr, no results\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references item not in policy -> non-zero exit, error to stderr\");\n  it.todo(\"claim with more damages of a type than covered -> non-zero exit, claim rejected\");\n  it.todo(\"claim with negative amount -> non-zero exit, error to stderr\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI reads JSON scenario from stdin and writes results JSON to stdout\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909175814},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me run the tests first to confirm they're green."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01T5o7v51r42gV19pEoYW4rT","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":3716,"output":149,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13569,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909175815,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-04a9af30-7bc8-4632-a02f-15b4958b4491","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01T5o7v51r42gV19pEoYW4rT","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (38 tests | 27 skipped) 3ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  11 passed | 27 todo (38)\n   Start at  16:06:19\n   Duration  168ms (transform 28ms, setup 0ms, collect 27ms, tests 3ms, environment 0ms, prepare 49ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909179396},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All the tests are passing, so now I'm going through a refactoring process. Looking at the naming first—`quote` is clear for what it does, `componentBasePremium` accurately describes computing the base premium for a set of components, and the variable names like `basePremiumTotal` and `componentCounts` are straightforward. Now I'm diving into the `quote` function to evaluate its structure and see where improvements can be made.\n\nThe code is fairly readable overall. The `firstInsuranceSurcharge` naming works fine even though it assumes first-time insurance, which matches the test cases. There's no significant duplication, and while I could reduce the number of intermediate variables, the current approach aids clarity. The `priorContracts` and `customer` parameters aren't used yet, but I'm keeping them since they'll be needed for future tests.\n\nThe real opportunity here is extracting the base premium accumulation logic into its own helper function—something like `basePremium(items)`—to separate the concern of computing the base premium from applying the surcharge and fee. This would make the `quote` function simpler and reveal the intent more clearly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"All 11 tests pass. Now let me apply the refactoring process.\n\n## Refactoring Analysis\n\n### Step 1: Naming Evaluation (FIRST PRIORITY)\n- `quote` — produces a premium quote from items. Clear, fits intent. **Keep.**\n- `componentBasePremium(count)` — returns base premium for `count` alike components. Clear. **Keep.**\n- `firstInsuranceSurcharge` — accurately describes the newcomer surcharge. **Keep.**\n- The `quote` function currently mixes two concerns: (a) computing the base premium across main items + component blocks, and (b) applying surcharge/fee/rounding. Extracting (a) into a named helper `basePremium(items)` reveals intent better (Rule 2) and reduces `quote`'s element count (Rule 4).\n\n### Step 2: Initial APP Mass (`quote` function body)\n\n```\nlet basePremiumTotal = 0;                          assign 6, const 1\nconst componentCounts = {};                        binding 1, const 1(empty)\nfor (item of items)                                loop 5, binding 1\n  if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type))              cond 4, invoc 2\n    componentCounts[type] = (…?? 0)+1              assign 6, binding 2, invoc 1(+), const 1, cond 4(??)\n  else basePremiumTotal += BASE_PREMIUM[type] ?? 0 assign 6, binding 1, invoc 1, const 1, cond 4(??)\nfor (count of Object.values(componentCounts))      loop 5, binding 1, invoc 2\n  basePremiumTotal += componentBasePremium(count)  assign 6, invoc 2, binding 1\nconst firstInsuranceSurcharge = base * RATE        binding 1, invoc 1(*), binding 2\nreturn Math.ceil(base + surcharge + fee)           invoc 2, invoc 2(+×2), binding 3\n```\nApprox **Total Mass ≈ 96** (quote body).\n\n### Step 3–4: Apply Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) + Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)\n\nExtract the base-premium accumulation into a dedicated helper. This makes `quote` read as \"base premium → surcharge → fee → round\", and gives the loop-heavy logic a self-documenting name."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01RUq2hoDBbTBApfdNATJAy7","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edit":"\n<parameter name=\"oldText\">const componentBasePremium = (count: number): number => {\n  if (count === BLOCK_SIZE) return BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  return count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n};\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: Item[],\n  priorContracts: number\n): number => {\n  let basePremiumTotal = 0;\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      basePremiumTotal += BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    }\n  }\n  for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n    basePremiumTotal += componentBasePremium(count);\n  }\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge =\n    basePremiumTotal * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  return Math.ceil(basePremiumTotal + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};","newText":"const componentBasePremium = (count: number): number => {\n  if (count === BLOCK_SIZE) return BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  return count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIU