) → Rule 2 (names already clear) → Rule 3 (eliminated duplicate Set) → Rule 4 (fewer elements: one fewer constant).\n\n**Tests:** All 30 passing (8 todo untouched)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 30\nRecent changes: added claim() (per-damage deductible 100, high-enchantment>=8 reimburses 50%), insuranceSum() (sword 1000/amulet 600/staff 800/potion 400/components 250 each), and cap() (2x insurance sum). Note there are two separate component-type Sets (COMPONENT_TYPES for premium, COMPONENT_INSURANCE_TYPES for insurance value) and two base-value records - check for duplication.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 30\nRecent changes: added claim() (per-damage deductible 100, high-enchantment>=8 reimburses 50%), insuranceSum() (sword 1000/amulet 600/staff 800/potion 400/components 250 each), and cap() (2x insurance sum). Note there are two separate component-type Sets (COMPONENT_TYPES for premium, COMPONENT_INSURANCE_TYPES for insurance value) and two base-value records - check for duplication.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784909542736},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll analyze the implementation and tests, then refactor while keeping tests green."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01KtHuGvzX3dEeaiSFK2tC4D","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_