r)\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests pass):** ✅ 30 passing.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals intent):** Names are clear; structure is self-documenting.\n- **Rule 3 (No duplication):** The task note flags two candidates:\n  - **Two component-type Sets** — `COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\",\"moonstone\"])` and `COMPONENT_INSURANCE_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\",\"moonstone\"])` are **identical knowledge** (\"which item types are components\"). This is genuine duplication → **consolidate**.\n  - **Two base-value records** — `BASE_PREMIUM` (100/60/80/40) vs `INSURANCE_VALUE` (1000/600/800/400) hold **different values/knowledge** (premium rates vs insured worth). Merging them would couple unrelated concepts and hurt clarity (violates Rule 2). → **Keep separate.**\n\nThe safe, correct improvement is eliminating the duplicate component-type Set.\n\n### Step 3: APP Mass (the affected duplication)\n\n**Before** — two Set constants:\n```\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst COMPONENT_INSURANCE_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n```\nPer Set: 1 binding + 1 invocation(new Set) + 2 constants = 1 + 2 + 2 = 5. Two Sets = **10**.\n\n**After** — single shared Set: **5**. Mass change **10 → 5 (delta −5)**.\n\nApplying the change:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_0155gM9u1RQokL7vgUQBfP3j","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-00-47_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE = 250;\nconst COMPONENT_INSURANCE_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst itemInsuranceValue = (item: Item): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_INSURANCE_TYPES.has(item.type)) return COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE;","newText":"const COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE = 250;\n\nconst itemInsuranceValue = (item: Item): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) return COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE;"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty